{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:gadya.1.2", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "gadya.1.2"}, "paraphrase": "The knowledge of Brahman, the means to liberation, is to be taught repeatedly until firmly grasped, to a disciple who is calm, self-controlled, free from faults, obedient, devoted to the teacher, and longing for liberation, who has approached in the proper way.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:teacher-student-qualifications"], "practices": ["prc:guru-upasatti", "prc:sravana"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:gadya.1.6", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "gadya.1.6"}, "paraphrase": "The teacher is one able to argue and to answer, retentive, calm, self-controlled, compassionate, learned in scripture, unattached to enjoyments, having renounced all works, a knower of Brahman established in Brahman, free of pretence and pride, whose sole aim is to help others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:teacher-student-qualifications"], "terms": ["trm:guru", "trm:brahmanistha"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:gadya.2", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "gadya.2"}, "paraphrase": "A model dialogue: the disciple, asked who he is, answers with his birth and caste; the teacher shows that body, caste and rites belong to the not-self, and leads him to know himself as eternal, pure awareness in which the cognitions of the intellect appear and which is never itself an object.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "consciousness-mind"], "practices": ["prc:atma-vicara"], "concepts": ["cpt:saksin"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:gadya.3", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "gadya.3"}, "paraphrase": "Parisaṃkhyāna, for seekers who wish to destroy merit and demerit and to avoid new ones: one reflects that sound and the other objects are not-self, change and depart, while 'I' am of the nature of pure awareness, unconnected, changeless, not an object — thus detaching from them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:parisankhyana"], "practices": ["prc:parisankhyana"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:padya.1", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "padya.1"}, "paraphrase": "Action cannot remove ignorance, since it is not opposed to it; only knowledge removes ignorance; hence knowledge alone is the means to liberation and the renunciation of works follows.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "disputes": ["dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the doctrine is certain, the chapter placement is not.", "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:upadesa-sahasri:padya.18", "source": "src:upadesa-sahasri", "location": {"ref": "padya.18"}, "paraphrase": "In the chapter on 'tat tvam asi', Śaṅkara holds that once the meaning of the sentence is understood, the self is known as free from suffering; he rejects the view that one must further practise repeated meditation (prasaṅkhyāna) on the sentence for knowledge to become effective.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:prasankhyana", "trm:tat-tvam-asi"], "disputes": ["dsp:prasankhyana", "dsp:sravana-alone-liberates"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the opponent is often identified with Maṇḍana Miśra.", "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
